================================================================================
                    LEUKOCYTE INPUT DATA GENERATOR
================================================================================

OVERVIEW
--------
A Python script to generate synthetic AVI video files for the leukocyte 
tracking benchmark. Creates raw/uncompressed AVI videos with grayscale frames 
simulating microscopy cell images.

REQUIREMENTS
------------
- Python 3.6+
- NumPy library

Install: pip install numpy

QUICK START
-----------
Generate mini dataset:
    python3 generate.py synthetic --preset mini --out-dir input_data/mini --seed 42

Generate all sizes:
    for preset in mini small medium large extra-large; do
        python3 generate.py synthetic --preset $preset --out-dir input_data/$preset --seed 42
    done

Or use batch script:
    ./generate_all.sh

FILE FORMAT
-----------
AVI (Audio Video Interleave) - Raw/Uncompressed
- Video codec: Raw video (DIB/uncompressed)
- Color format: 8-bit grayscale (paletted)
- Palette: 256 grayscale entries (0-255)
- Frame rate: 30 fps (configurable)

PRESETS
-------
Preset        Width  Height  Frames  FPS  File Size  Description
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
mini          320    240     50      30   ~3.7 MB    Quick testing
small         480    360     150     30   ~25 MB     Small-scale testing
medium        640    480     600     30   ~185 MB    Reference dataset
large         800    600     1000    30   ~480 MB    Large-scale testing
extra-large   1024   768     1500    30   ~1.2 GB    Stress testing

USAGE
-----
Basic syntax:
    python3 generate.py <command> [options]

Commands:
    synthetic       Generate synthetic AVI video from scratch

PARAMETERS
----------
Required:
    --out-dir PATH          Output directory (created if needed)

Optional:
    --preset NAME           Preset configuration (default: medium)
                            Choices: mini, small, medium, large, extra-large
    --width INT             Override frame width in pixels
    --height INT            Override frame height in pixels
    --frames INT            Override total number of frames
    --fps INT               Override frames per second (default: 30)
    --seed INT              Random seed for reproducibility (default: 42)
    --overwrite             Overwrite existing output files

PARAMETER DETAILS
-----------------
--preset NAME
    Selects predefined configuration:
    - mini: Fast generation, small file, good for development
    - small: Moderate size for quick experiments
    - medium: Reference size matching original datasets
    - large: Extended testing scenarios
    - extra-large: Comprehensive testing and stress tests

--width INT and --height INT
    Frame dimensions in pixels. Must be positive integers.
    Width is automatically padded to 4-byte alignment.

--frames INT
    Total number of frames in video. More frames = larger file.
    Example: 600 frames at 30 fps = 20 seconds of video

--fps INT
    Frames per second (frame rate). Standard value is 30 fps.
    Does not affect file size, only playback speed.

--seed INT
    Random seed for deterministic generation. Same seed = identical videos.
    Use different seeds to create variations.

--overwrite
    Replace existing files. Without this, generator errors if file exists.

EXAMPLES
--------
Example 1: Generate mini dataset
    python3 generate.py synthetic \
        --preset mini \
        --out-dir input_data/mini \
        --seed 42
    
    Output: input_data/mini/testfile.avi (320×240, 50 frames, ~3.7 MB)

Example 2: Generate medium dataset (reference)
    python3 generate.py synthetic \
        --preset medium \
        --out-dir input_data/medium \
        --seed 42
    
    Output: input_data/medium/testfile.avi (640×480, 600 frames, ~185 MB)

Example 3: Custom dimensions
    python3 generate.py synthetic \
        --preset small \
        --width 512 \
        --height 384 \
        --frames 200 \
        --out-dir input_data/custom \
        --seed 100
    
    Output: input_data/custom/testfile.avi (512×384, 200 frames)

Example 4: Generate all standard sizes
    for preset in mini small medium large extra-large; do
        echo "Generating $preset..."
        python3 generate.py synthetic \
            --preset $preset \
            --out-dir input_data/$preset \
            --seed 42
    done

Example 5: Overwrite existing file
    python3 generate.py synthetic \
        --preset mini \
        --out-dir input_data/mini \
        --seed 42 \
        --overwrite

Example 6: Different seed for variation
    python3 generate.py synthetic --preset mini --out-dir input_data/mini_v1 --seed 42
    python3 generate.py synthetic --preset mini --out-dir input_data/mini_v2 --seed 123

