RUNNING THE BENCHMARK
---------------------
After generating input data, run the leukocyte tracking benchmark:

Basic usage:
    ./leukocyte <num_frames> <num_threads> <input_avi_file>

With output file:
    ./leukocyte <num_frames> <num_threads> <input_avi_file> -o <output_file>

Examples:

Mini dataset:
    ./EX1_optimized_codes/leukocyte_gcc 5 4 input_data/mini/testfile.avi -o output_mini.txt

Small dataset:
    ./EX1_optimized_codes/leukocyte_gcc 15 4 input_data/small/testfile.avi -o output_small.txt

Medium dataset:
    ./EX1_optimized_codes/leukocyte_gcc 50 4 input_data/medium/testfile.avi -o output_medium.txt

Large dataset:
    ./EX1_optimized_codes/leukocyte_gcc 100 4 input_data/large/testfile.avi -o output_large.txt

Extra-large dataset:
    ./EX1_optimized_codes/leukocyte_gcc 150 4 input_data/extra-large/testfile.avi -o output_extra-large.txt

Benchmark parameters:
    num_frames      Number of frames to process (≤ total frames in video)
    num_threads     Number of OpenMP threads to use
    input_avi_file  Path to input AVI video file
    -o output_file  (Optional) Path to save tracking results

ADVANCED USAGE
--------------
Verifying generated files:
    Check file properties:
        ffprobe -v error -show_format -show_streams input_data/mini/testfile.avi
    
    Check file size:
        ls -lh input_data/*/testfile.avi

Synthetic frame generation:
    The generator creates realistic microscopy cell images with:
    1. Background Noise: Random grayscale values (intensity 20-60)
    2. Cell Objects: 3-8 circular cells per frame
       - Random radius: 15-40 pixels
       - Random intensity: 80-200
       - Positioned in central region
    3. Texture: Gradient patterns within cells
    4. Motion: Frame-to-frame displacement simulating cell movement

Performance tips:
    - Generation time proportional to frame count and resolution
    - Memory usage scales with frame count
    - Use --seed for reproducible results

File size calculation:
    Approximate formula:
        size (bytes) ≈ width × height × frames + overhead
        size (MB) ≈ (width × height × frames) / (1024 × 1024)
    
    Example for medium preset:
        640 × 480 × 600 = 184,320,000 bytes ≈ 175.8 MB
        + AVI headers ≈ 185 MB total

TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------
Error: "File already exists"
    Solution: Add --overwrite flag or delete existing file

Error: "Invalid dimensions"
    Solution: Ensure width and height are positive integers

Error: "Invalid frame count"
    Solution: Ensure frames is a positive integer

Low performance:
    - Reduce --frames or use smaller --width and --height
    - Ensure sufficient RAM (especially for extra-large preset)

NOTES
-----
- Generated videos use raw/uncompressed format matching original datasets
- Frame width is automatically padded to 4-byte alignment per AVI spec
- All frames stored in bottom-up bitmap format (standard for AVI)
- 256-color grayscale palette ensures compatibility with benchmark
- Generation is fully deterministic when using same seed value

